1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,577
Two roads climb the same hill.

2
00:00:02,577 --> 00:00:06,883
Road one rises three metres for
every ten metres you ride forward.

3
00:00:07,283 --> 00:00:10,959
Road two rises one metre for
every two metres forward.

4
00:00:10,959 --> 00:00:12,606
Which road is steeper?

5
00:00:13,056 --> 00:00:16,852
Aarav has to pick one on his
bicycle, on the way to college.

6
00:00:17,202 --> 00:00:18,776
Just looking is not enough.

7
00:00:18,776 --> 00:00:20,649
He needs one number that decides.

8
00:00:21,149 --> 00:00:23,314
That one number is called the slope.

9
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:24,400
Let us find it.

10
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,286
Think of a ramp.

11
00:00:26,286 --> 00:00:29,850
As you move along it, you
go across, and you go up.

12
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,651
The distance across is called the run.

13
00:00:32,651 --> 00:00:35,155
The height you gain is called the rise.

14
00:00:35,555 --> 00:00:40,780
Slope is rise divided by run: how much
you go up for every one step across.

15
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,280
Road one.

16
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,762
Three divided by ten is zero point three.

17
00:00:45,162 --> 00:00:46,062
Road two.

18
00:00:46,017 --> 00:00:48,757
One divided by two is zero point five.

19
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,779
Bigger slope, steeper road.

20
00:00:50,779 --> 00:00:51,957
Road two wins.

21
00:00:52,607 --> 00:00:56,278
Now let us put a line on graph
paper, and turn it slowly.

22
00:00:56,678 --> 00:01:01,406
The angle the line makes with the x
axis, measured anticlockwise, is called

23
00:01:01,406 --> 00:01:02,564
its inclination.

24
00:01:02,564 --> 00:01:03,889
We call it theta.

25
00:01:04,289 --> 00:01:06,463
At zero degrees the line is flat.

26
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:08,158
It does not rise at all.

27
00:01:08,158 --> 00:01:09,058
Slope zero.

28
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,067
As the line tips up, the slope grows.

29
00:01:12,067 --> 00:01:15,266
At forty five degrees,
the rise equals the run.

30
00:01:15,266 --> 00:01:16,166
Slope one.

31
00:01:16,525 --> 00:01:18,759
Near ninety degrees the slope shoots up.

32
00:01:18,759 --> 00:01:19,659
Ten.

33
00:01:19,185 --> 00:01:20,085
Twenty.

34
00:01:19,737 --> 00:01:20,724
Over a hundred.

35
00:01:20,724 --> 00:01:23,000
At ninety, the line stands straight up.

36
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,205
Now the run is zero, and we
can never divide by zero.

37
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:29,260
So the slope is not defined.

38
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:32,970
Past ninety, the line
falls as it goes right.

39
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:35,247
Negative rise, so negative slope.

40
00:01:35,847 --> 00:01:40,603
In a right triangle, tan theta is
the opposite side over the side next

41
00:01:40,603 --> 00:01:41,503
to theta.

42
00:01:41,472 --> 00:01:43,220
That is rise over run.

43
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:44,967
So m equals tan theta.

44
00:01:45,617 --> 00:01:47,942
Now take two points on a line.

45
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:49,667
P is x one, y one.

46
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,392
Q is x two, y two.

47
00:01:51,792 --> 00:01:52,692
Step one.

48
00:01:52,574 --> 00:01:57,298
Draw a right triangle under the line,
going across from P, then up to Q.

49
00:01:58,048 --> 00:01:58,948
Step two.

50
00:01:58,863 --> 00:02:00,870
The run is the change in x.

51
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,828
That is x two minus x one.

52
00:02:03,578 --> 00:02:04,478
Step three.

53
00:02:04,466 --> 00:02:06,465
The rise is the change in y.

54
00:02:06,465 --> 00:02:08,368
That is y two minus y one.

55
00:02:09,118 --> 00:02:10,088
Step four.

56
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:15,596
So m equals y two minus y one, over
x two minus x one, when x one and x

57
00:02:15,596 --> 00:02:17,078
two are different.

58
00:02:17,828 --> 00:02:18,885
Side by side.

59
00:02:18,885 --> 00:02:21,360
This line goes up as you move right.

60
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,405
Positive rise, positive slope.

61
00:02:23,405 --> 00:02:25,215
Theta is less than ninety.

62
00:02:25,615 --> 00:02:28,247
This line goes down as you move right.

63
00:02:28,247 --> 00:02:30,339
Negative rise, negative slope.

64
00:02:30,339 --> 00:02:32,190
Theta is more than ninety.

65
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:33,690
Your turn.

66
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:36,769
A line passes through
two, five and six, one.

67
00:02:36,769 --> 00:02:39,005
Is its slope positive or negative?

68
00:02:39,005 --> 00:02:40,245
Pause and decide.

69
00:02:43,445 --> 00:02:44,345
Negative!

70
00:02:44,251 --> 00:02:48,261
As x grows from two to six,
y drops from five to one.

71
00:02:48,261 --> 00:02:50,330
Rise minus four, run four.

72
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:51,635
Slope minus one.

73
00:02:52,285 --> 00:02:53,321
Remember this.

74
00:02:53,321 --> 00:02:54,966
Slope is rise over run.

75
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:57,406
Going up to the right means positive.

76
00:02:57,406 --> 00:02:59,139
Going down means negative.

77
00:02:59,839 --> 00:03:01,219
Two special lines.

78
00:03:01,219 --> 00:03:04,591
A flat line, like the
x axis, has rise zero.

79
00:03:04,591 --> 00:03:06,251
So its slope is zero.

80
00:03:06,651 --> 00:03:09,989
A standing line, like
the y axis, has run zero.

81
00:03:09,989 --> 00:03:11,962
So its slope is not defined.

82
00:03:12,562 --> 00:03:13,462
Quick one.

83
00:03:13,357 --> 00:03:16,545
A line passes through
three, one and three, seven.

84
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:17,815
What is its slope?

85
00:03:17,815 --> 00:03:18,938
Pause and think.

86
00:03:22,138 --> 00:03:23,098
Not defined!

87
00:03:23,098 --> 00:03:25,443
Both points have x equal to three.

88
00:03:25,443 --> 00:03:28,807
The line stands straight
up, and the run is zero.

89
00:03:29,457 --> 00:03:31,147
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:31,497 --> 00:03:35,589
Find the slope and the inclination
of the line through minus one, two,

91
00:03:35,589 --> 00:03:37,071
and three, minus two.

92
00:03:37,571 --> 00:03:38,471
Step one.

93
00:03:38,408 --> 00:03:39,308
The rise.

94
00:03:39,245 --> 00:03:42,206
y two minus y one is minus two minus two.

95
00:03:42,206 --> 00:03:43,676
That is minus four.

96
00:03:44,426 --> 00:03:45,326
Step two.

97
00:03:45,293 --> 00:03:46,193
The run.

98
00:03:46,107 --> 00:03:49,279
x two minus x one is
three minus minus one.

99
00:03:49,279 --> 00:03:50,421
That is four.

100
00:03:51,171 --> 00:03:52,088
Step three.

101
00:03:52,088 --> 00:03:54,609
The slope m is minus four over four.

102
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:55,995
That is minus one.

103
00:03:56,745 --> 00:03:57,645
Step four.

104
00:03:57,608 --> 00:04:01,239
tan theta is minus one, so
theta is more than ninety.

105
00:04:01,239 --> 00:04:04,196
Theta is one hundred
and thirty five degrees.

106
00:04:04,846 --> 00:04:06,307
Now, the exam trap.

107
00:04:06,657 --> 00:04:09,387
Slope through one, two and four, eight.

108
00:04:09,387 --> 00:04:14,246
Many students take y two minus y one
on top, but x one minus x two below.

109
00:04:14,246 --> 00:04:15,146
Minus two.

110
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:18,268
But the order must match, top and bottom.

111
00:04:18,268 --> 00:04:19,407
Six over three.

112
00:04:19,407 --> 00:04:22,891
The slope is plus two, and
the line clearly goes up.

113
00:04:23,541 --> 00:04:24,904
Where is this asked?

114
00:04:24,904 --> 00:04:29,416
In JEE Main, for example in January
twenty nineteen: find a missing coordinate

115
00:04:29,416 --> 00:04:31,530
from the slope through two points.

116
00:04:32,130 --> 00:04:33,226
Exam level now.

117
00:04:33,226 --> 00:04:37,351
The line through A and B makes one
hundred and thirty five degrees with

118
00:04:37,351 --> 00:04:38,261
the x axis.

119
00:04:38,261 --> 00:04:39,161
Find k.

120
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:40,072
Pause and solve.

121
00:04:45,472 --> 00:04:46,995
The answer is B.

122
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,023
Minus one.

123
00:04:48,523 --> 00:04:52,625
The slope is tan of one hundred and
thirty five degrees, which is minus

124
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,525
one.

125
00:04:53,586 --> 00:04:58,599
From the two points, the slope is
two k minus three, over four minus k.

126
00:04:58,599 --> 00:05:00,655
Set that equal to minus one.

127
00:05:01,155 --> 00:05:05,772
So two k minus three equals k
minus four, and k is minus one.

128
00:05:05,772 --> 00:05:08,908
Check: minus five over five is minus one.

129
00:05:09,508 --> 00:05:11,048
Here is your recap.

130
00:05:11,048 --> 00:05:12,630
Screenshot this card.

131
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:18,016
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

132
00:05:18,416 --> 00:05:19,316
One.

133
00:05:18,869 --> 00:05:22,909
What is the slope of a line that
goes up three for every two across?

134
00:05:23,809 --> 00:05:24,709
Two.

135
00:05:24,278 --> 00:05:27,036
Why is the slope of
the y axis not defined?

136
00:05:27,936 --> 00:05:28,836
Three.

137
00:05:28,432 --> 00:05:30,433
A line has inclination sixty degrees.

138
00:05:30,433 --> 00:05:31,564
What is its slope?

139
00:05:32,664 --> 00:05:37,741
Next time: two roads that never meet,
and two that cross perfectly square.

140
00:05:37,741 --> 00:05:39,698
Their slopes hide a secret.

141
00:05:39,698 --> 00:05:41,902
Parallel and perpendicular lines.
